WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 line:92%
-You are a millennial mayor

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a town in Indiana,
South Bend.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're very popular,
it would seem, by most polls,

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.843
but also, I think,
people maybe living in New York

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
or across the country
don't realize

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:12.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's a very diverse city
that you represent.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You've had some successes.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.550
You've also had some issues
with poverty, homelessness.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-What part of being a mayor

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:23.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you think is --
will sort of impose itself

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
on being the job
of president the most?

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think what you learn
when you're a mayor

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:33.066
is that your job is not only
to come up with good policies,

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
also to run
an administration capably,

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also
just to hold people together

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to make sure
that you're calling people

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.440 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to their highest values.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that might be the part
that we're most missing

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.444 line:92%
in the White House right now.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:47.147
And if we want to deal
with our toughest issues,

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.648 line:92%
we have to have that attitude.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:49.949 line:92%
So, in a place like South Bend,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
still a largely
low-income community

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of the departure
of the auto industry

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.122 line:92%
that started in the '60s,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've been able
to reduce poverty,

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've been able to put
a lot of resources

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
into dealing with things
like homelessness.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.930
But you can't pretend that those
problems have just gone away.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:07.901
And I guess, you know,
at the national level, you know,

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
the president thinks
that when there's a problem,

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can just say the opposite
and will it away,

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether it's North Korea or
whether it's a domestic issue.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.777
But when you're in a community,
there are no alternative facts.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:22.115
If there's a problem that
persists from a hole in the road

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:22.749 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to a homelessness issue,

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.085
you have to just continue
calling people together

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.720 size:81% position:41%
to work on it with you
until it gets better.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wanted
to ask about this, as well.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:29.956 line:92%
During your announcement,

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:32.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were onstage
with your husband, Chasten.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this must have been --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, this is an incredible
moment for anyone.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
For anyone to be
with their partner on that day

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
must be a special moment,
but to think that

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:48.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
only four years ago,
gay marriage was not legal,

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.043 line:92%
did that day have a special,

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
even added element,
to it for you?

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:54.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. If nothing else,
it's just a reason to believe.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.016
Even at this dark
and complicated and bleak moment

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
in American politics,
it's a reason to be hopeful.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, running for office
is an act of hope.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't do it
unless you believe

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.491 line:92%
that it's at least possible,

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:08.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
using all of the mechanics
of the political system

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.062 line:92%
to make better things happen.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as somebody
whose marriage exists

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:15.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
because nine women and men
sat and took a vote,

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:18.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
and by the grace of one vote,
we get to be married now.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
I understand how
the decisions that are made

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
in those big white buildings
really affect our lives.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:25.512
The idea that at the beginning
of this decade, I had a choice.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could either be out
or I could be in the military.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:30.950
I could either be out or
I could run for elected office.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
At least that's
how I viewed it at the time.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the idea that
just a few years later,

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
I announced a campaign
for the American presidency,

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.425
and my husband comes out
on the stage to be with me

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.495
after I do it, just shows you
what's possible in this country.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a wonderful thing
to watch.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.931 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:50.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is mind-blowing to me.
You --

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are the youngest person,
as of now,

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.008
running for president, but more
people are joining every day,

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
so don't...
-You never know.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, don't think
you've got that one for life.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:01.814 size:75% position:38%
Also, Bernie Sanders
is the oldest person

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:02.916 line:92%
currently running for president.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.983 line:92%
When you were 18 years old,

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:08.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
you won an essay in 2000,
writing about Bernie Sanders.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And there you wore --

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a -- I would call that
a high school cut.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.427 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.696
-Thank you for sharing that
photo with the American people.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really appreciate that.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:20.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it must be surreal
to you now to --

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.936
Obviously, Bernie was someone
who was influential to you

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:27.440
back then, to be sort of in
the same sphere as him now.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I mean,
I wrote that essay --

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like someone
who claims to have discovered

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:33.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
a band before they were cool.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was an obscure
Congressman from Vermont,

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.016
and I just thought there was
something really compelling

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:39.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the way he said what he
believed at a time

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.621
when it didn't feel like we had
a lot of that in politics.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I wrote it up,
and I won that essay contest.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is a little strange
to be competing with him now,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.762
but frankly, a lot of the people
I'm competing with

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
are people I admire.
I'm not --

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:54.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't view this process
right now as having opponents

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.502 line:92%
as much as it has competitors.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:59.639
And we can have a lot in common,
at the same time,

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.007 line:92%
have rather different messages

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be very different
messengers.

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.143 line:92%
-My favorite thing about it is,

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:07.413 size:75% position:38%
it sounds like a way
he could burn you.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.648 line:92%
Like, "I was a congressman

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you were writing essays
about me!"

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.852 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
That would probably be the way
he would say it

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:17.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
if he also
was being nice about it.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.458 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:21.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a photo
that went around.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, you're running
for president,

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.797 size:81% position:41%
but you're still doing
your duties as mayor.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.499
Tell us what's happening
in this photo right here.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:27.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
This is a really fun one.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I got to the office early,
which is rare.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:30.970 line:92%
I was knocking out some work.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
I stepped out into the hallway
to use the bathroom,

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.408
and the elevator opened,
and this couple turned up

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said, "Mayor!"
This is exactly

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:40.146
the kind of moment that my staff
tries to avoid, right?

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.547 line:92%
That I'm alone, you know,

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.350
interacting with people
accosting me, wanting something.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.351 line:92%
But, like, when you're mayor,

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to have time
for everybody.

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And, you know,

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was trying to be polite
by letting them know

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:50.857 line:92%
I didn't have a lot of time,

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.125 size:84% position:42%
and then they explained
why they were there.

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:55.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was on her way
to get a C-section at 9:00.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.329 line:92%
This must've been about 8:15.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said, "I want to tell
mom all the news at once,

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:01.200 size:84% position:42%
so we were wondering
if you could marry us."

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-So, I thought,

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:05.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wait.
I can make time for that."

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.240 line:92%
So we came into the office.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.076 size:81% position:41%
I found a staff member
who found some ribbon.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
They hadn't had time
to get a ring,

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we took ribbon
and made a little --

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.782
made little rings out of it,
and I knocked out, you know,

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:18.551
"By the powers vested in me,
by the state of Indiana..."

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.620 size:84% position:42%
knocked out the wedding
in about 20 minutes,

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.988
and then sent them on their way
to the hospital.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:25.391
And later, we got a picture of
them with a really healthy kid,

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we're just
so happy for them.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:33.766
I also like -- I like that
an Indiana mayor's office

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
does look like the set
of "Parks and Recreation."

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:39.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I do -- I do enjoy that.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:42.608
Definitely, he's wearing
Andy costume right there.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:43.142 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:46.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, everybody,
that's mayor Pete Buttigieg.

